# CSS Styling
## Use ?url for Explicit Stylesheet Links [#](https://tanstack.com/start/v0/docs/framework/react/guide/css-styling#use-url-for-explicit-stylesheet-links)
```
// src/routes/__root.tsx
/// <reference types="vite/client" />
import { createRootRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'
import appCss from '../styles/app.css?url'

export const Route = createRootRoute({
  head: () => ({
    links: [{ rel: 'stylesheet', href: appCss }],
  }),
})
```

## Know When CSS Is Discovered [#](https://tanstack.com/start/v0/docs/framework/react/guide/css-styling#know-when-css-is-discovered)
Because Start already knows about these stylesheets before route loaders run, they can be sent in the static Early Hints phase as rel=preload; as=style links.

Start sees that stylesheet only when route head() returns the link, which happens after router.load().

